+---
+id: task-003-paolo-welcome-coupon-refused-as-already-used-after-cancel-and-reorder-same-day
+type: task
+title: "Paolo: welcome coupon refused as already used after cancel-and-reorder same day"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Report
+
+Paolo, a customer, placed an order with his one-time welcome code, cancelled it the same day (wrong
+size), then placed a corrected order with the same code. The code was refused as already used.
+
+## Investigation
+
+This is exactly the single-use-coupon give-back bug already fixed on `main` in `src/orders.ts`
+(`cancel`): it used to call `this.#coupons.giveBack(order.coupon, order.customer)`, but
+`Coupons#usedBy` records the order **id** that used a code (`this.#coupons.use(request.coupon, id)`
+in `place`), so give-back could never match and the coupon stayed locked forever. That call now reads
+`this.#coupons.giveBack(order.coupon, order.id)`, and `test/orders.test.ts` ("gives a single-use
+coupon back when the order that used it is cancelled") covers it end to end: place with a single-use
+coupon, cancel, re-place with the same coupon, assert it is accepted and marked used by the new order.
+
+I reproduced Paolo's exact scenario (place with a single-use coupon, cancel the same day, re-place
+with the same coupon) against the current code: the second order is accepted and the coupon is freed.
+`npm test` passes (20/20). No code change was needed.
+
+## Outcome
+
+No bug on current `main`. Reply to Paolo: the welcome code is usable again after the cancellation; if
+he still sees it refused, the shop needs to check it is running this version of the order service.
